# Second input graph for LexMalta__recipes__recipe-importer_rdflib_extras_infixowl.py__BooleanClassExtentHelper___call____getExtent
# -- added by the mutation audit (2026-10-31). Assigned to
# Individual.factoryGraph by driver.py, like fixture.ttl.
#
# Covers the two shapes fixture.ttl lacks, both of which the real infixowl
# callers meet:
#   - a blank-node subject: an anonymous class expression
#     `[ owl:unionOf (...) ]`, the usual form of a union in OWL, where the
#     BooleanClass identifier is a BNode (kills a mutant that keeps only
#     IRI subjects);
#   - one subject carrying owl:unionOf twice: `g.subjects(p)` yields it once
#     per triple (rdflib 7.2.1, unique=False), so the region yields two
#     BooleanClass for ex:c5 (kills a mutant that deduplicates the subjects).
# ex:c6 is a neighbour that must not match (owl:intersectionOf).
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

ex:c4 rdfs:subClassOf [ owl:unionOf ( ex:m5 ex:m6 ) ] .
ex:c5 owl:unionOf ( ex:m7 ) , ( ex:m8 ex:m9 ) .

# neighbour that must NOT match: different predicate
ex:c6 owl:intersectionOf ( ex:m4 ) .
